  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-005">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:administers" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-firewall" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Annotation of the source assignment; no universal or existential property restriction is asserted.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:qualification>The target can comprise multiple deployed components. Presence and management exclusions remain in the source requirements.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source assigns maintenance, monitoring, and security control of the named target to the Gray AW.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u010.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-006">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:administers" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-management" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Annotation of the source assignment; no universal or existential property restriction is asserted.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:qualification>The target can comprise multiple deployed components. Presence and management exclusions remain in the source requirements.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source assigns maintenance, monitoring, and security control of the named target to the Gray AW.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u010.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-007">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:may_be_realized_as" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-virtual-machine" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Optional realization only. The host and VM are separate entities.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source permits an AW to be a VM on a physical host/server dedicated to AW VMs.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u004.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-008">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:may_be_realized_as" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-physical-workstation" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Optional realization only; no AW-to-physical-device subclass is asserted.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source permits a physical-workstation AW and applies dedicated-function restrictions to that realization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p011:u009.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u004.s004" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-009">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:hosts" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-aw-host" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-virtual-machine" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The annotation does not identify the physical host with the VM or AW.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:qualification>The referenced VMs are AW VMs. The source prohibits cohosting the listed enrollment, provisioning, registration, and SIEM VMs.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The host/server houses VMs used as AWs.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u004.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u004.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-010">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:performs_role" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-macsec-device" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-supplicant" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The function is retained separately from its device bearer; no subtype is asserted.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source requires each MACsec Device to perform the supplicant function during the described authentication process.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u006.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-011">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:performs_role" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-macsec-device" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-authenticator" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The function is retained separately from its device bearer and from the Authentication Server.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source requires each MACsec Device to perform the authenticator function during the described authentication process.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u006.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-012">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:supports_authentication" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-authentication-server" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-macsec-device" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The annotation does not identify the server with a supplicant or authenticator.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The MSC Authentication Server supports EAP-TLS mutual authentication between MACsec Devices.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u006.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u006.s003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-013">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:distributes_keys_to" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-key-server" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-macsec-device" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The target is the peer in the applicable MACsec pair; no universal relation to every MACsec Device is asserted.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The designated Key Server distributes Secure Association Keys to the other MACsec Device.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u013.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-014">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:example_of_role_realization" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-root-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-trust-anchor-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Certificate-level example supports a role association only. It does not make every Root CA a Trust Anchor CA or equate the categories.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The certificate-chain passage gives a Root CA certificate as an example Trust Anchor certificate.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s005" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s006" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s007" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-015">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:may_perform_role" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-encryption" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-perimeter-device" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Conditional on the Outer Firewall being absent. No unconditional subclass is asserted.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>An Outer Encryption Component may serve as a perimeter device when no Outer Firewall is present.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p023:u009.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-016">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:may_be_realized_as" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-screening-router" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-customer-edge-router" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Example only. No Customer Edge Router subclass of Screening Router is asserted.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source gives an existing Customer Edge Router as an example screening-router realization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u010.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u010.s004" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u010.s005" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-017">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:may_be_realized_as" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-encapsulation-device" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-router" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Source-scope issue REQ-I01 remains unresolved; the annotation does not settle universal Solution Component membership.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:qualification>The standalone device is conditional. Encapsulation may instead be a feature of an encryption component.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>A separate standalone router or switch can provide the required encapsulation when the selected encryption component lacks the feature.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u007.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u007.s003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-018">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:may_be_realized_as" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-encapsulation-device" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-switch" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Source-scope issue REQ-I01 remains unresolved; the annotation does not settle universal Solution Component membership.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:qualification>The standalone device is conditional. Encapsulation may instead be a feature of an encryption component.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>A separate standalone router or switch can provide the required encapsulation when the selected encryption component lacks the feature.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u007.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u007.s003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-019">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:collects_logs_from" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-red-siem" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-encryption" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The association records the source configuration without asserting deployment or a property restriction.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source assigns collection and analysis of the named target logs to the Red SIEM.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u004.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
